Power gloves: Because once you have "wishes to spare", you don't need an 
offensive punch.  And if you really want an offensive punch, wish for 
Grayswandir, which gets better over time, instead of worse.

For combat, DEX gloves are a joke.  All they offer is increased chance to 
hit, which you can get tons of simply by gaining levels and boosting 
luck.  Exception: SDSM-wearing monks will benefit from them (although 
maxing level and luck works too).

It turns out that (according to my reading of the source) DEX gloves are 
pretty good for spellcasters, because the only factors that affect spell 
to-hit seem to be monster AC, player DEX, and player spell skill.  But 
they still wouldn't be in my first 10 wishes.

